  "question": {
    "text": "A wire is made by attaching two segments together end to end. One segment is made of aluminium and the other is of steel. The effective coefficient of linear expansion of the two-segment wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the fractional length of aluminium is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;are the least positive integers, then what is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>? (linear coefficients of thermal expansion of aluminium and steel are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, respectively)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The change in length of wire <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </msub> <msub> <mi>&#160;&#945;</mi> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </msub> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mtext>st</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mi>&#160;&#945;</mi> <mtext>st</mtext> </msub> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;associated with a temperature change of <math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;where <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </msub> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mrow> <mtext>St</mtext> </mrow> </msub> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;are the coefficient of linear expansion of aluminium and steel, respectively<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mrow><mtext>A</mtext><mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mspace></mspace><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><msup><mtext>C</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mtext>St</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mspace></mspace><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><msup><mtext>C</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />The effective coefficient of linear expansion of the two segments of wire <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>9</mn> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mo>/</mo> <msup> <mspace></mspace> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> <mtext>C</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </msub> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mtext>St</mtext> </msub> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </mfrac> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mtext>st</mtext> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mrow> <mtext>A</mtext> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo> </mrow> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi>l</mi><mo>&#8289;